#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:5
#: ca0403528c48406eafd2898747cad4fe
msgid "Battery Failsafe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:6
#: 87fc96384f9047158344d22e3b4059d0
msgid "The battery failsafe can be configured to automatically switch the vehicle into SURFACE mode or disarm if the vehicle battery voltage drops below a specified voltage for 10 seconds or the estimated remaining capacity has dropped below a configurable threshold."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:10
#: d5cf5517175242ad8a9481eff25638a2
msgid "This failsafe requires the vehicle have a working :ref:`Power Module <common-powermodule-landingpage>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:12
#: e76df26d7dfe430cab28ea8a90ae00ac
msgid "ArduPilot supports up to 9 batteries/power monitors. The discussion below applies to those optional batteries also. Each can trigger a failsafe and each can have different actions and setup values. In addition, a group of batteries can be treated as a single unit, see ``BATTx_MONITOR`` = 10."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:15
#: 475b380b14b1429e88ffc6b4ed177271
msgid "When the failsafe will trigger"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:16
#: eaca3b40783e4123bcffffcf39a0407f
msgid "If enabled and set-up correctly the battery failsafe will trigger if the main battery's:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:18
#: 391e24f161c34a69a958be8580ce7705
msgid "voltage drops below the voltage held in the :ref:`BATT_LOW_VOLT <BATT_LOW_VOLT>` parameter (or FS_BATT_VOLTAGE in older versions) for more than 10 seconds. The default voltage is 10.5 volts. If set to zero, the voltage based trigger will be disabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:19
#: 05bc142c9d9b491fa4be570cb7995493
msgid "remaining capacity falls below the :ref:`BATT_LOW_MAH <BATT_LOW_MAH>` parameter (or FS_BATT_MAH in older versions) 20% of the battery's full capacity is a good choice (i.e. \"1000\" for a 5000mAh battery). If set to zero, the capacity based trigger will be disabled (i.e. only voltage will be used)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:22
#: 4a138a35bc5144c59b801ad0aa1356a7
msgid "What will happen"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:23
#: a7ad56273d614a648b5603485e47640b
msgid "When the failsafe is triggered:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:25
#: 610025c67b2e498db50ef9b0cd77dacd
msgid "Buzzer will play a loud low-battery alarm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:26
#: 64c7dfdfac054673ba4f647e80fce9ca
msgid "LEDs will flash yellow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:27
#: 72abd0430e1f430bbab14043b79d1e82
msgid "\"Low Battery!\" will be displayed on the ground station's HUD (if telemetry is connected)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:29
#: 8613aca7435b4aacab3d6464cf810f7a
msgid "Then one of the following will happen, depending on :ref:`BATT_FS_LOW_ACT<BATT_FS_LOW_ACT>`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:31
#: e3723bc6b4ef432fa977d48dfb361f16
msgid "**Nothing**  (value 0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:32
#: b48c0e08b2a942cb8f58c6d05282e5a3
msgid "**Disarm motors** (value 1)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:33
#: ba7d5db9364846e1adbd58ff8178d2d3
msgid "**Enter SURFACE mode** (value 2)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:35
#: 0a6a7739004245039926d61ae7cc0655
msgid "As with all failsafes, the user can re-take control of the vehicle by changing the flight mode switch to another mode. The battery failsafe will not trigger again unless the two-layer failsafe is setup (see below)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:39
#: 24a2d78c9f9348d49f130682a2e2a436
msgid "Once a battery failsafe has triggered, it cannot be reset until the autopilot is rebooted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:42
#: 701061de64234b11bf89486f6ab5b09d
msgid "Setting up using Mission Planner"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:43
#: 6fc356396cff409186cfdd3ba702aa33
msgid "On the **INITIAL SETUP \\| Mandatory Hardware \\| Failsafe** page:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:45
#: 8f78528c7da6481f98e32e097e491eaa
msgid "If the Battery section parameters are greyed out follow instructions to setup the :ref:`Power Module <common-powermodule-landingpage>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:46
#: b1c4726e061046a5bbc7db6466112dac
msgid "Set the \"Low Battery\" threshold voltage (i.e. 10.5 volts)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:47
#: d3f1efa9132944bf8da43b68b9552053
msgid "Set the \"Reserved MAH\" or leave as \"0\" if the failsafe should never trigger based on estimated current consumed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:48
#: 1c2c161a1b9741bfa8e85bfca8905772
msgid "Select the desired behavior (Land, RTL, SmartRTL, etc) from the drop-down list"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:54
#: 9df68063d9c94948b467bb049501f670
msgid "Two-Layer failsafe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:55
#: c8f1935ac6f4423f863fc2d3f0d60861
msgid "ArduPilot includes a two-layer battery failsafe. This allows setting up a follow-up action if the battery voltage or remaining capacity falls below an even lower threshold."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:57
#: 282d70b7c1634212b9d71c3880f21a50
msgid ":ref:`BATT_CRT_VOLT <BATT_CRT_VOLT>` - holds the secondary (lower) voltage threshold. Set to zero to disable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:58
#: 81c611c5f6084334b36f98ff20a7d364
msgid ":ref:`BATT_CRT_MAH <BATT_CRT_MAH>` - holds the secondary (lower) capacity threshold. Set to zero to disable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:59
#: 3ea5e409f80b43a289431908e6f1d01d
msgid ":ref:`BATT_FS_CRT_ACT <BATT_FS_CRT_ACT>` - holds the secondary action to take."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:62
#: fb152b0d7aae416fb440e960beffd501
msgid "Advanced Settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:64
#: b2d517d0eb2644d3a8d828ae63599cf0
msgid ":ref:`BATT_FS_VOLTSRC <BATT_FS_VOLTSRC>` allows configuring whether the raw battery voltage or a sag corrected voltage is used"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:65
#: ba5798c414ff482c81fb169f69c2ddce
msgid ":ref:`BATT_LOW_TIMER <BATT_LOW_TIMER>` can configure how long the voltage must be below the threshold for the failsafe to trigger"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:66
#: 1ceba0106bc741d7925997e684307996
msgid "``BATTx_`` parameters can be setup to trigger the failsafe on other battery monitors."
msgstr ""
